Ladybird shifts the remaining own indices of a sparse backing store
when an observable array removes its first slot. V8 uses HasProperty
and DeleteProperty in GenericArrayShift(). SpiderMonkey checks for a
hole with HasAndGetElement() in array_shift(). JavaScriptCore calls
shift() from arrayProtoFuncShift() to move the remaining properties.

Chrome 158.0.8127.36, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5 agreed on the
returned values, lengths, and own indices for empty arrays, runs of
holes, and present undefined elements before and after a hole.
